<PageLayout title="Content policy" description="The content policy of Lone Voice." updated="22 November 2026">
  <p>
    This page explains what Lone Voice publishes and the standards I hold it to. It is a personal blog, written
    by one person, and these are promises I make to myself and to readers.
  </p>

  <h2>What is published</h2>
  <p>
    Everything here is my own writing and my own opinions: personal notes, essays, photographs and links to
    things I found worth sharing. Nothing is paid for, and the blog carries no advertising or sponsored posts.
    If that ever changes, the post will say so clearly.
  </p>

  <h2>What is not published</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Hate, harassment, or attacks on people for who they are.</li>
    <li>Anything that exposes another person's private details, or my own.</li>
    <li>Material that is illegal, or that encourages harm to anyone.</li>
    <li>Writing, photographs or other work copied from others without permission or credit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Other people's work</h2>
  <p>
    Quotations are short and credited. Photographs and images are mine, or used with permission, or credited
    to their source. A link to another site is not an endorsement of that site or of everything on it, and
    I don't control what it publishes.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections and changes</h2>
  <p>
    If I get something wrong, I will fix it. When a post is meaningfully changed after it was published,
    the post shows an updated date, so you can tell it was edited.
  </p>

  <h2>Not advice</h2>
  <p>
    This blog is a personal record of what I think and feel. It is not professional, medical, legal or financial
    advice, and it should not be treated as such.
  </p>

  <h2>Comments and contact</h2>
  <p>
    There are no comments on this blog, so there is nothing for readers to moderate or report here. Anyone can
    follow new posts through the RSS feed.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, this page will be updated first, and the date at the top will change with it.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
